# --- Optional: Web Push Notifications ---------------------------------
#
# Web Push lets the app send browser notifications even when closed.
# Three parts must be set up for it to work:
#
# 1. Client-side (this file):
#    Generate a VAPID key pair:
#      npx web-push generate-vapid-keys
#    Paste the public key below. The private key stays secret.
#
# 2. Supabase Edge Function secrets (Dashboard → Settings → Edge Functions):
#    Add these three secrets:
#      VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY  = <same public key>
#      VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY = <the private key from step 1>
#      VAPID_SUBJECT     = mailto:admin@yourdomain.com
#
# 3. Deploy the edge functions after setting secrets:
#      supabase functions deploy admin-send-push
#      supabase functions deploy cron-push-checkin-reminder
#
# Without these keys, push notifications are silently disabled.
VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=sb_publishable_LXWMmCRNLd00hZmzj3OK9g_UiXn50-I


# --- Anti-spam: Cloudflare Turnstile -----------------------------------
#
# Protects the public, unauthenticated write paths: organization registration,
# the contact form, and (via Supabase's built-in captcha setting) signup,
# sign-in and password reset.
#
# 1. Create a widget at https://dash.cloudflare.com → Turnstile.
#    Add your production domain AND localhost for local development.
# 2. Put the SITE key here (safe to ship — it appears in the page source):
VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
#
# 3. Put the SECRET key in Supabase → Settings → Edge Functions → Secrets as
#    TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY. Never put the secret in this file: anything prefixed
#    VITE_ is bundled into the client and is public.
# 4. Optionally set TURNSTILE_ALLOWED_HOSTNAMES alongside it, comma-separated,
#    e.g. openhrapp.com,www.openhrapp.com — Cloudflare reports which hostname
#    solved the challenge, and anything outside the list is rejected. This is
#    what stops a token minted on someone else's page being replayed at our
#    endpoint. Defaults to the production domains if unset; add localhost only
#    if you want the widget working against cloud functions in development.
# 5. To also protect auth endpoints, enable Supabase → Authentication →
#    Settings → Enable CAPTCHA protection, provider "Turnstile", and paste the
#    same secret there.
#
ALLOW_EMPTY_CONTENT=1
# Leaving VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY empty hides the widget and the edge function
# skips verification, so local development works without a Cloudflare account.
